  "name": "power_text_cases",
  "description": "How a power is written, the same in Python (summary.power_text / share_text) and TypeScript (beam.ts): contract optical_layout_v2.md §12.3. Not a trace fixture. A case with `mw` (an absolute power in mW) expects the number and unit (the description puts 'arriving ' / '入射 ' in front); a case with `p` (power relative to the source) expects the whole share text. sig3(x), x > 0: e = the largest exponent in [-15, 15] with POW[e] <= x, POW[e] = the double of the literal '1e{e}' (-15 below that); n = floor(x / POW[e-2] + 0.5); n >= 1000 -> n = 100, e += 1; the value is n x 10^(e-2). Absolute: 0 -> '0 mW'; 0 < mw < 1e-12 (below 0.001 pW) -> '< 0.001 pW', without sig3 (so sig3 is only used for e >= -12 and POW[e-2] is always in the table); else the unit exponent u is the largest of 3 (W), 0 (mW), -3 (µW), -6 (nW), -9 (pW) not above e, and n x 10^((e-2)-u) is written with digits only: k >= 0 appends k zeros, k < 0 puts in a decimal point and drops trailing zeros and a trailing point - no float formatting. Relative: X = p x 100; X <= 0 -> '0 %' (a negative floating-point residue is 0); 0 < X < 0.001 -> '< 0.001 %'; else the digits of sig3(X) (k = e - 2, no unit), as '相对 X %' / 'relative X %'.",
